From: Lume Retro OS
Subject: [PATCH] udev joypad: open the pad read-only when it cannot be written

The pads of the consoles are read-only for the games (device-fixes D16,
P-87): the user that runs the games is in the input group and could inject
events by writing to an evdev node, so lume-input's virtual gamepad and the
built-in controls are 0640. Upstream opens every pad with O_RDWR (for the
force feedback writes) and gives up when that fails, so RetroArch saw no pad
at all and no game read the buttons.

When O_RDWR fails, try O_RDONLY: the pad works, only the force feedback (a
write) is lost, and the virtual gamepad has none.

--- a/input/drivers_joypad/udev_joypad.c
+++ b/input/drivers_joypad/udev_joypad.c
@@ -129,8 +129,12 @@
    unsigned long evbit[NBITS(EV_MAX)]   = {0};
    unsigned long keybit[NBITS(KEY_MAX)] = {0};
    unsigned long absbit[NBITS(ABS_MAX)] = {0};
    int fd = open(path, O_RDWR | O_NONBLOCK);

+   /* Lume: a read-only pad (no write for the games) still works,
+    * without force feedback */
+   if (fd < 0)
+      fd = open(path, O_RDONLY | O_NONBLOCK);
    if (fd < 0)
       return fd;

